  "rotationNote": "The two engines compose the same euler triple in different orders (ours applies X then Y then Z; the reference applies Z then X then Y -- 0.745 apart in the composed matrix for (20,40,65) degrees). The rotated cells therefore author [43.9234191172, 1.9598266612, 58.4462037256] on our side, which reproduces the reference's own evaluated matrix under our composition to 1.1e-16, so these cells compare action centres and not euler conventions. The order gap itself is a separate finding.",
